course: dictionary
lesson: 9388
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word spread can mean to open something out, to put a layer on something, or to move into more places. Context tells you which meaning is right. «Spread your arms» means open them wide, but «spread butter on toast» means put a thin layer on the toast.
explain: Look at the words around it. «A cobra spreads its hood» shows the snake opening its hood wide as a warning. «The fire spread» means it moved into more places, and quickly.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Germs spread through coughs and sneezes» means germs move from person to person, so covering your mouth when you cough really matters.
fact: Spread can be a verb or a noun: you can spread butter, or you can eat a spread.
fact: «Spread» can mean to open or stretch out, as in «spread your arms».
fact: «Spread» can mean to move into more places or reach more people, as in «germs spread» and «the fire spread».
fact: «Spread» can mean to share out over time or space, as in «spread the work over a week».
fact: In maths, data spread means how far apart the numbers are.
exercise: A cobra spreads its hood to warn others. What does spreads mean here? | Moves into more places | Shares out over a week | *Opens out wide | Puts a thin layer on
exercise: «The fire spread quickly through the dry grass.» What does spread mean? | Opened out wide | Ate a big meal | Put a thin layer over | *Moved into more places
exercise: Maya says «spread the work over a week». What does spread mean here? | *To share it out over time | To stretch out the arms | To put butter on it | To make the work bigger
test: What does spread mean in «spread butter on toast»? | To share out over time | *To put a thin layer on | To stretch out wide | To move into more places
test: What does spread mean in «Germs spread through coughs and sneezes»? | To share out a snack | To put a layer on a surface | To open out wide | *To reach more people
exam: In «a jar of hazelnut spread», what kind of word is spread? | A verb, to share out over time | *A noun, a soft food for bread | A verb, to move into more places | A verb, to open wide
